  "source": { "doc": "CV3000.pdf", "page": 5, "section": "How to Order" },
  "note": "Extracted by hand from the How to Order schematic on pages 5 and 6. The code reads prefix CV, then model (full or reduced port), size, body, then the seventeen character positions grouped 1&2 ends, 3&4 insert/trim, 5&6 seat, 7&8 packing, 9&10 handle, 11&12 operation, 13&14 positioner, 15-17 fail position. The CV prefix is folded into the model code (CV3000F or CV3000R). Confirmed with John: (1) the insert position offers only the six codes the schematic prints (A1/A2/A3/S1/S3/R1); the size-specific slot inserts in the Cv vs travel tables are not offered here and would need Marwin sign-off; (2) Siemens is named on the positioners, since it is a third-party accessory openly listed in the public datasheet, not a PCT white-label valve OEM; (3) three constraints are enforced: 4 inch is reduced port only, a fail open or closed position needs a spring-return actuator, and the 2-IQ positioner's double-acting and spring-return variants must match the actuator.",
